唐霍的精神境界？
Don Ho?

149
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:07,680
是的，唐霍
Right. Don Ho.

150
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:16,660
麦克，唐霍是唱<小泡泡>的 夏威夷歌手
Mike, Don Ho is the Hawaiian singer who recorded Tiny Bubbles.

151
00:09:19,140 --> 00:09:21,220
对，非常高尚
Right. Very spiritual guy.

152
00:09:37,371 --> 00:09:40,641
他已经坚持了46分钟! 这次能成功!
He's up to 46 minutes now! We're going to do it!

153
00:09:40,674 --> 00:09:42,874
成功？成功扭伤臀部？
Do what? Throw out his hip?

154
00:09:43,460 --> 00:09:47,320
不，破连续模仿猫王的纪录
No, break the worlds record for the most consecutive hours of imitating Elvis!

155
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:50,500
这不是模仿，这是折磨
I take it you're going for endurance here, not accuracy.

156
00:09:52,660 --> 00:09:54,620
还需多久才能破纪录？
How much longer before he gets in the book?

157
00:09:55,155 --> 00:09:57,185
-现在几点？ -1点半
- What time is it now? - 1 :30.

158
00:09:57,860 --> 00:09:59,080
需要到周四往后一周
A week from Thursday.

159
00:10:01,395 --> 00:10:02,696
凯罗
Carol.

160
00:10:02,763 --> 00:10:04,167
本!
Ben!

161
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:06,480
虽然猫王很感动.
I'm sure Elvis would be touched but...

162
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:10,520
但总不能这样下去12天
you can't keep this up for another 12 days.

163
00:10:10,837 --> 00:10:12,173
本？
Ben?

164
00:10:13,380 --> 00:10:14,820
猫王死了
The King is dead.

165
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,080
对不起
I'm sorry.

166
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:22,420
怎样了？
How do you feel?

167
00:10:23,060 --> 00:10:24,620
★我非常震惊
I'm all shook up

168
00:10:29,660 --> 00:10:30,860
★我非常震惊
I'm all shook up

169
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:36,980
-测试完成没有？ -完成了
- So, did you finish scoring our tests yet? - Yeah.

170
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:40,900
-结果如何？ -其中一项是你缺乏耐性
- Well, what's it say? What's it say? - For one thing, it says you're impatient.

171
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:44,000
杰森，别这样 我们到底合得来吗？
Oh, come on, Jason. Are we compatible or not?

172
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:45,580
-我合得来，你不行 -去你的
- I am. You're not. - Darn.

173
00:10:47,474 --> 00:10:50,949
你自己看吧，我们的分数很高
No, go ahead. See for yourself. We got an excellent score.

174
00:10:51,220 --> 00:10:52,680
差不多完全吻合
Agreed on just about everything.

175
00:10:53,347 --> 00:10:55,752
特别是猥亵的问题
Especially the smutty questions.

176
00:10:56,950 --> 00:10:58,700
这有一条不吻合
Heres one we disagreed on.

177
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:00,380
“你的爱好是什么？”
"What is your favorite hobby? "

178
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:02,340
-杰森.. -怎么了？
- Oh, Jason. - What?

179
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:05,680
我答“园艺”，你答“收集棒球卡片”
I said "gardening, " and you said "collecting baseball cards."

180
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:08,320
我们的婚姻出现裂缝了
How can we go on with this rift in our marriage?

181
00:11:08,420 --> 00:11:09,100
无法继续了
It's impossible.

182
00:11:10,497 --> 00:11:13,334
我们得卖掉房子，瓜分孩子
Well have to sell the house and divide the kids.

183
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:14,680
麦克给你了
You take Mike.

184
00:11:16,670 --> 00:11:19,405
这一题你又答错了
Heres another one you screwed up.

185
00:11:20,060 --> 00:11:21,900
“你睡在床的哪一边？”
"What side of the bed do you sleep on? "

186
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:24,420
我答“左边”，你答“左边”
I said "the left" and you said "the left."

187
00:11:24,580 --> 00:11:25,440
其实没有错
Well, that's right.

188
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:28,500
你睡在床的左边，我睡在你的左边
You take up most of the bed, and I sleep on what's left.

189
00:11:30,780 --> 00:11:34,200
又一题答错了
Oh, no, heres another one you botched up.

190
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:35,880
杰森，答问题要认真点
Jason, you should be more careful.

191
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:38,560
“你会对配偶有所隐瞒吗？”
"Would you ever keep anything from your spouse? "

192
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:40,440
我答什么了？
What did I say?

193
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:42,720
你答“会”
You said "yes."

194
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:46,000
我就是这个意思
Well, that's what I meant.

195
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:48,431
什么？
What?

196
00:11:54,220 --> 00:11:57,120
你怎么隐瞒我了？
What do you mean, you'd keep things from me?

197
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:59,220
那等于你骗我
That's like saying that you'd lie to me.

198
00:11:59,220 --> 00:12:01,240
不，别弯曲我的题目
No, no, you're twisting my answer.

199
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:05,620
问题是“你会对配有有所隐瞒吗？”
The question simply asks, "Would you ever keep anything from your spouse? "

200
00:12:05,986 --> 00:12:08,050
题目的范围很广呢
"Anything" is a big word.

201
00:12:08,220 --> 00:12:10,060
任何事情都不能隐瞒
It means anything.

202
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:14,160
谢谢你的解释
Well, thanks for clearing that up.

203
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:16,620
那么告诉我骗子的意思是什么？
Now will you tell me what "liar" means?

204
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:20,400
拜托，麦姬，别小题大做
Come on, Maggie, what are you making such a big deal of this for?

205
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:22,220
我坦诚对你
I've always been honest with you.

206
00:12:23,036 --> 00:12:24,064
是吗？
Oh?

207
00:12:24,404 --> 00:12:25,569
是的
Yes.

208
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:28,460
还记得有人在你的果汁机上 放泥巴吗？
Remember when somebody tried to mix cement in your blender?

209
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:34,300
我立刻挺身而出说“是本干的”
I stepped forward right away and said, "Ben did it."

210
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:38,280
杰森，这一点都不好笑
Jason, you think this is funny, don't you?

211
00:12:38,380 --> 00:12:39,700
亲爱的，我只是说.
No, honey, I'm just saying--

212
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:41,160
我也记得.
Well, I'll tell you what I remember.

213
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:43,540
我记得在马塔酒店.
I remember the Mattapoisett Inn.

214
00:12:44,057 --> 00:12:47,120
那是我们蜜月的地方
The.... Yes, where we had our honeymoon.

215
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:48,960
是的，回想第一个晚上.
Yes, now remember that first night...

216
00:12:48,980 --> 00:12:51,280
我们坐在干柴烈火前.
and remember in front of the fireplace when we sat--

217
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:53,940
亲爱的，火炉旁的事我都记得
Honey, I remember what we did in front of that fireplace.

218
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:56,600
你说了些什么？
Remember what you said?

219
00:12:56,820 --> 00:12:58,940
我说过“再来一次”
Yes, I said, "Lets try that again...

220
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:02,700
“这次不用冰块”
"without the ice cubes."

221
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:09,200
你还说坦诚是幸福婚姻的关键
You also said that total honesty is essential to a happy marriage.

222
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:11,820
结婚后我还这样说？
I said that after we we're married?

223
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:17,360
好吧，我是说过
Okay, okay. I said that.

224
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:19,420
但我们现在更加成熟了
But we're more mature now.

225
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:22,060
所以我们就能睁眼说白话
So, now we lie like rugs.

226
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:27,600
不，只是某些事情不会主动说出来
No, I'm only saying that there are some things that I might not volunteer.

227
00:13:28,460 --> 00:13:31,340
什么事情？给我一个例子
Well, like what things? Give me an example.

228
00:13:31,820 --> 00:13:32,460
例子？
An example?

229
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:35,600
两列火车，相向而行.
Two trains, traveling from opposite directions--

230
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,560
-杰森 -火车A时速85英里.
- Jason. - Train A moving 85 miles an hour--

231
00:13:37,611 --> 00:13:39,413
我说生活中的例子
I meant an example from our lives.

232
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:41,440
我还没说完，我们坐在火车B上
Well, you didn't let me finish. We we're on train B.

233
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:43,600
去你的，别说笑了
Damn it, be serious.

234
00:13:45,060 --> 00:13:47,120
-你要严肃的例子？ -是的
- You want a serious example? - Yes.

235
00:13:48,488 --> 00:13:49,858
好吧
Okay.

236
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:54,100
这件事不告诉你是不想让你生气
Here's something I didn't tell you because I thought it might upset you.

237
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:56,800
我不会生气的
I will not be upset.

238
00:13:59,366 --> 00:14:03,603
几周前我在洗衣店碰见阿里森了
A couple of weeks ago I ran into Alison Van Dyke at the dry cleaners.

239
00:14:03,620 --> 00:14:05,460
-你的旧女朋友？ -是的
- Your old girlfriend? - That's the one.

240
00:14:05,660 --> 00:14:06,700
太好了
How nice.

241
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:09,500
怎么不告诉我碰见阿里森了？
Now, why wouldn't you want to tell me you ran into Alison?

242
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:12,100
-不知道，我觉得你会.. -不高兴？
- I don't know, maybe I thought you"d-- - Be upset?

243
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:15,540
胡说，她现在还卖肉吗？
Nonsense. Does she still strip for money?

244
00:14:18,540 --> 00:14:20,520
麦姬，她是艺术模特
Maggie, she's an artist's model.

245
00:14:20,580 --> 00:14:22,360
那么她去洗衣店干嘛？
And what does she have to dry-clean, anyway?

246
00:14:22,522 --> 00:14:25,997
把自己塞到洗衣机里？
You'd think they could just hose her down once a week.

247
00:14:26,820 --> 00:14:30,280
之所以不告诉你嘛
See, this is exactly why I didn't want to tell you.

248
00:14:30,630 --> 00:14:33,536
我不高兴不是因为你碰见她
Oh, no, I'm not upset that you saw her.

249
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:35,480
而是因为你隐瞒我
I'm upset that you hid it from me.

250
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:37,640
你跟那个一丝不挂的说些什么了？
So, what did you and the nudist talk about?

251
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:42,900
我就是应该隐瞒你
See, I knew I that I should've kept this to myself.

252
00:14:43,620 --> 00:14:46,580
对!隐瞒你那些肮脏的秘密
Right! That and all your other squalid, little secrets.

253
00:14:46,940 --> 00:14:50,420
失陪了，我出去散步
Well, if you'll excuse me. I'm off to do a little jogging, Jason.

254
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:59,180
看完今晚是不能做第37条了
Well, I guess that means no Number 37 tonight.

255
00:15:04,580 --> 00:15:07,040
累了，饿了，闷了
I'm tired. I'm hungry. I'm bored.

256
00:15:07,300 --> 00:15:10,580
我要去厕所，真讨厌 你也很讨厌
I have to go to the bathroom. I'm sick of this. I'm sick of you.

257
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:13,420
这就对了，继续说说讨厌什么
That's the spirit! Tell me more. Tell me what you hate.

258
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:15,600
什么都讨厌，我讨厌这房子.
I hate everything. I hate this house.

259
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:18,140
讨厌这地毯，这沙发垫，这桌子
I hate this rug, this sofa cushion, this table.

260
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:19,900
我讨厌他的睡衣
I hate his pajamas.

261
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,600
-他是怎么了？ -他要破牢骚的纪录
- What's with him? - He's going for a record in complaining.

262
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:25,760
他要发牢骚连续62小时
He has to complain for 62 straight hours.

263
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:27,560
目前已经连续2分钟了
So far, he's got two straight minutes.

264
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:31,600
我讨厌分钟，我讨厌手表 我讨厌你的脸
I hate minutes. I hate stopwatches. I hate your face.

265
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:35,200
我就让你好好讨厌
I'll give you something to complain about.

266
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:38,160
我讨厌被个子大的人殴打
I hate getting beat up by people bigger than me.

267
00:15:39,380 --> 00:15:41,060
我讨厌疼痛
I hate pain.

268
00:15:43,260 --> 00:15:46,220
本，到楼上寻找讨厌的东西吧
Ben, lets go upstairs and find something for you to hate.

269
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:47,940
我讨厌楼梯
I hate stairs.

270
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:50,480
我讨厌这个钟，我讨厌这些蜡烛.
I hate this clock, and I hate these candles and....

271
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:57,800
麦克，准备好上第一堂课没？
Hi, Mike. Ready for the first class?

272
00:15:58,118 --> 00:16:00,955
林达，不是说在课堂见吗？
Lynda, look, I said I'd meet you down at the karate place.

273
00:16:01,180 --> 00:16:03,720
我知道，但一起走路上学更有趣
Oh, I know. I just thought it'd be more fun if we walked together.

274
00:16:05,625 --> 00:16:08,633
不是吗？我不能来这里？
Was I wrong? It is okay that I'm here, isn't it?

275
00:16:08,660 --> 00:16:10,820
不，我带你参观我家
Yeah. Look, why don't I give you a tour of the house.

276
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:14,580
这是厅里的壁厨
This is the hall closet here.

277
00:16:19,260 --> 00:16:21,120
-爸爸 -麦克
- Hey, Dad. - Hi, Mike.

278
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:25,960
你妈妈散步回来没有？
Your mother come back from her jog yet?

279
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:27,060
还没有
No, not yet.

280
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:32,340
-还以为听到她声音呢 -不，不是她
- I thought I heard her voice. - No, Dad, that wasn't her.

281
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:38,300
麦克，空手道的事你还是坦白吧.
Mike, you know, there's no use in you and I discussing this karate thing anymore...

282
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:39,460
多说无益
unless you're gonna be straight with me.

283
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:41,720
班上肯定是有女孩子
Now, I still think there's a girl in this class.

284
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:43,540
不可能
No way, Dad.

285
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:47,720
好吧，是有这么一个
All right. Well, maybe there is one girl.

286
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:50,780
但这女孩奇坏无比
But we're talking flea collars and milk bones.

287
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:55,440
这女孩是头猪
This girl is the Elephant Girl.

288
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:07,040
西弗先生，幸会
Nice to meet you, Mr. Seaver.

289
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:13,320
谁说黛比是畜生了？
You thought Debbie DiZomba was an animal.

290
00:17:25,205 --> 00:17:26,233
嗨
Hi.

291
00:17:28,742 --> 00:17:29,770
嗨
Hi.

292
00:17:31,660 --> 00:17:34,340
别管我，我进来找眼镜在不在
Don't let me disturb you. I just think I left my glasses in here somewhere.

293
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:40,320
在
So you did.

294
00:17:43,623 --> 00:17:44,856
谢谢
Thanks.

295
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:46,360
不客气
Don't mention it.

296
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:49,360
行了，不打扰你了
Well, that's all I wanted. I won't bother you any more.

297
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:50,800
不打扰
It's no bother.

298
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:55,280
其实我有一小时空闲时间 若有话要说.
In fact, I have a free hour if there's anything you'd like to discuss...

299
00:17:57,140 --> 00:17:58,020
西弗太太.
Mrs. Seaver.

300
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,040
医生.
Well, Doctor...

301
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:05,320
我有些烦恼
there is something troubling me.

302
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:06,700
我知道
I knew it.

303
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:09,860
我是个心理医生，我有这种触觉
I'm a psychiatrist. I sense these things.

304
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:13,160
可以说说看吗？
Would you like to sit down and tell me about it?

305
00:18:18,320 --> 00:18:19,680
是我的丈夫
It's my husband.

306
00:18:21,820 --> 00:18:23,980
-他怎样了？ -他行事荒谬
- What about him? - He's impossible.

307
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:27,280
我很爱他，他是个好父亲 但有时候.
I mean, I love him, and he's a great father, but sometimes--

308
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:30,160
-他打你了？ -没有
- Does he beat you? - No.

309
00:18:31,460 --> 00:18:35,080
-他酗酒？他在公共场所裸露？
Drink to excess? Scratch himself in public?

310
00:18:36,543 --> 00:18:37,708
没有
No.

311
00:18:38,220 --> 00:18:39,840
那怎么个行事荒谬？
Then why is he so impossible?

312
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:42,700
他不完全坦白
Because he doesn't believe in total honesty.

313
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:47,160
西弗太太，你现在完全坦白了吗？
Mrs. Seaver, are you being totally honest with me now?

314
00:18:47,787 --> 00:18:48,918
是的
Yes.

315
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:52,060
有个确保的方法
Well, there's one sure way to find out.

316
00:18:53,993 --> 00:18:55,329
催眠
Hypnosis.

317
00:18:57,297 --> 00:18:58,701
催眠？
Hypnosis?

318
00:18:58,900 --> 00:19:01,700
盯着这个催眠器
You just keep your eye on the hypnotic trance inducer.

319
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:03,940
厉害
Very impressive.

320
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:06,360
可以看看花式表演吗？
Now may I see you do Walk the Dog.

321
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,840
表演要收钱的，西弗太太
Not for these prices, Mrs. Seaver.

322
00:19:11,760 --> 00:19:13,280
你感到很疲惫
Now you're getting tired.

323
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:16,910
眼睛睁不开了
You can barely keep your eyes open.

324
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:17,980
你睡着了
You're out.

325
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,220
万试万灵
Works every time.

326
00:19:23,540 --> 00:19:27,480
西弗太太，你现在不能说谎了
So, Mrs. Seaver, you are now incapable of telling a lie.

327
00:19:28,140 --> 00:19:31,900
你说的将会都是真话
And everything you say will be the complete and absolute truth.

328
00:19:31,965 --> 00:19:33,680
-知道吗？ -知道了
- You understand? - Yes, Doctor.

329
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:35,900
首先简单测试一下
All right. Well start with a simple test question.

330
00:19:37,120 --> 00:19:41,040
你认为丈夫的红色格子亲衫如何？
What do you really think of your husband's red plaid blazer?

331
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:45,360
他的红色格子亲衫？
His red plaid blazer?

332
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:49,580
跟他的牙肉颜色.
Well, I think that it really brings out the color of his...

333
00:19:50,650 --> 00:19:51,815
很相称
gums.

334
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:56,720
全部都要是真话
The whole truth, Mrs. Seaver.

335
00:19:58,200 --> 00:20:01,220
那是除了卡在洗手盘的 那条凯罗的蛇以外.
I think it's the ugliest thing I've seen since Carol's snake...

336
00:20:01,220 --> 00:20:02,320
我所见最恶心的东西
got caught in the dishwasher.

337
00:20:04,560 --> 00:20:06,260
很好，这才像样
Good. Now we're getting somewhere.

338
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:09,100
加上那条领带.
And that awful tie he wears with it.

339
00:20:09,100 --> 00:20:11,440
简直像活在杂货店里的人
Makes him look like a thrift shop blew up in his face.

340
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,800
我只是问亲衫的事
I only asked about the blazer.

341
00:20:16,100 --> 00:20:17,280
我只是诚实回答
Just being honest.

342
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:19,360
我很高兴你喜欢这样
Well, I'm glad you're enjoying this.

343
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:21,820
西弗太太，我还有一个问题
I have one more question for you, Mrs. Seaver.

344
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:25,900
去年圣诞派对，马蒂是不是.
By any chance, at last year's Christmas party...

345
00:20:25,900 --> 00:20:28,300
追求你了？
did Marty Brandt make a pass at you?

346
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:32,520
-你怎么知道？ -我怎么知道不重要
- How did you know-- - Well, it doesn't matter how I found out.

347
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:34,100
他是不是追求你了？
Did he make a pass at you, or not?

348
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:36,800
是的
Well, yes.

349
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:40,180
不过没什么，算不上追求
But it was nothing. I wouldn't even call it a pass.

350
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:43,520
他邀你去南太平洋度假
He asked you to go to Tahiti with him.

351
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:45,940
周末而已
Just for the weekend.

352
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:49,700
你怎么不告诉我？
Well, why didn't you tell me?

353
00:20:50,260 --> 00:20:52,340
丈夫不应该知道.
I mean, doesn't a husband have a right to know...

354
00:20:52,340 --> 00:20:53,740
妻子鬼混的事？
when his wife is propositioned?

355
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:57,200
杰森，我认为没必要说出来
Jason, I didn't think there was any point in mentioning it.

356
00:20:58,120 --> 00:21:01,320
我不想破坏你和马蒂的友谊
I mean, honey, I didn't want to ruin your friendship with Marty.

357
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,480
而且，马蒂当时喝醉了
Besides, Martyd had too much to drink.

358
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:05,880
-他不知道自己在干什么 -我知道
- He didn't know what he was doing. - I know.

359
00:21:06,340 --> 00:21:09,640
因为他被拒后，蹒跚来找我
Because as soon as you turned him down, he staggered over to me...

360
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:11,940
含含糊糊都说出来了
and blabbed the whole sordid story.

361
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:14,540
马蒂告诉你了？
Marty told you?

362
00:21:15,080 --> 00:21:16,000
他坦白了
He confessed.

363
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:21,080
接着他哭了 还要用我的领带擦鼻子
Then he broke into tears and tried to blow his nose on my tie.

364
00:21:22,780 --> 00:21:25,260
就是称红亲衫那条
The one I wear with my red plaid blazer.

365
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:28,780
杰森，对不起
Jason, I'm sorry.

366
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:31,960
我应该告诉你的
I should have told you.

367
00:21:32,986 --> 00:21:34,151
也许吧
Maybe.

368
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:39,080
也许你认为说出来有百害而无一利
Or maybe you realized that telling me wouldn't do anybody any good...

369
00:21:39,080 --> 00:21:40,680
于是就一言不发
so you kept it to yourself.

370
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:43,120
我欣赏你这一点
I admire you for that.

371
00:21:43,630 --> 00:21:45,034
是吗？
Really?

372
00:21:45,620 --> 00:21:48,920
若是马蒂没喝醉酒 你早就告诉我了
And I'm sure if Marty had been sober, you would have told me everything.

373
00:21:49,860 --> 00:21:51,700
度假回来就会马上告诉我
As soon as you got back from Tahiti.

374
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:57,660
若是阿里森没穿衣服 你也会告诉我
And I'm sure you would have told me if Alison had been nude.

375
00:22:00,420 --> 00:22:02,380
度假回来马上告诉你
Right after we got back from Tahiti.

376
00:22:04,183 --> 00:22:05,211
杰森
Jason.

377
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:08,800
西弗医生，谢谢你
I mean, Dr. Seaver. Thank you.

378
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:10,940
-你帮了我很大的忙 -是的
- You've been very helpful. - Yes.

379
00:22:11,820 --> 00:22:14,100
这次心理治疗效果显著
Well, it has been a most productive session.

380
00:22:14,540 --> 00:22:17,320
我有事想要试验一下
However, there's one other thing I'd like to try with you.

381
00:22:18,260 --> 00:22:20,580
我从来没对病人试验过的
Something I've never tried before with a patient.

382
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:21,620
试验什么？
What's that?

383
00:22:25,738 --> 00:22:27,142
第42题
Number 42.

384
00:22:27,974 --> 00:22:29,207
医生
Doctor.

385
00:22:29,375 --> 00:22:32,600
你被催眠的，无法抗拒
There is no use resisting. You're under hypnosis.

386
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:33,460
谁抗拒了？
Who's resisting?

387
00:22:43,289 --> 00:22:45,592
世界纪录的人收到信后.
When those world record people get this letter...

388
00:22:45,625 --> 00:22:47,996
肯定会让我们入围
well be in that next edition for sure.

389
00:22:48,027 --> 00:22:49,931
你们破了什么纪录？
So, what record did you guys break?

390
00:22:49,962 --> 00:22:54,097
一天内尝试破纪录最多次的纪录
Most failed attempts trying to get into the World Record Book in one day.

391
00:22:55,435 --> 00:22:58,272
这种纪录是不成立的
And they said it couldn't be done.

392
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:03,240
爸爸，妈妈，我可以学现代舞蹈吗？
Mom, Dad, can I take modern dance?

393
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:55,755
[zeroxia@gmail.com] 2006.03.12
